# Third-party notices for @oh-my-cybersecurity/attack-playbook-core

This package carries an absorbed MITRE ATT&CK execution corpus assembled from one
upstream community project. It is licensed under the MIT License. The notice and
permission text is reproduced below, as the license requires of any copy or
substantial portion.

The corpus shipped with this package is JSON generated from the pin below.

## atomic-red-team

- Upstream repository: https://github.com/redcanaryco/atomic-red-team
- Pinned commit: a0e3f9bc69fed2fd711bd1f1aa87a40c33482fe6
- License: MIT
- Copyright line: Copyright (c) 2018 Red Canary, Inc.
- Upstream LICENSE file: https://github.com/redcanaryco/atomic-red-team/blob/a0e3f9bc69fed2fd711bd1f1aa87a40c33482fe6/LICENSE.txt

Derivation: `attack_technique`, `display_name`, and every entry of
`atomic_tests[]` - name, `auto_generated_guid`, description, `supported_platforms`,
`input_arguments`, `dependency_executor_name`, `dependencies`, `executor`, and
`manual` - are read from the `atomics/T*/T*.yaml` technique files at that pin and
mapped onto the `Technique`, `AtomicTest`, `AtomicExecutor`, `AtomicDependency`,
and `InputArgument` shapes in `src/types.ts`. The upstream YAML is not vendored
here by this package; only generated JSON derived from it ships.

